\date{2024-08-12}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{The Regensburg extension of the fundamental theorem of identity types}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\import{common}
\meta{source}{[agda-unimath/foundation.regensburg-extension-fundamental-theorem-of-identity-types](https://unimath.github.io/agda-unimath/foundation.regensburg-extension-fundamental-theorem-of-identity-types.html)}


\p{
Given a type-family #{B \colon A \to \universe{U}} on a pointed type #{a : A} and a subuniverse \universe{P}, if the total type #{{\sigma-type{x:A}{B(x)}}} is \universe{P}-separated then every family of maps
##{f \colon \pi-type{x : A}{(a = x) \to B(x)}}
has fibers in \universe{P}. If, moreover, #{A} is connected this is a biimplication.
}
